  "formula_html": "<p><strong>Add VAT:</strong> <code>VAT = Net &times; (Rate / 100)</code> and <code>Gross = Net + VAT</code>.</p><p><strong>Remove VAT:</strong> <code>Net = Gross / (1 + Rate / 100)</code> and <code>VAT = Gross - Net</code>. Never multiply Gross directly by the VAT rate.</p>",
  "faqs": [
    {
      "q": "Why doesn't removing 20% VAT equal multiplying gross by 0.80?",
      "a": "Because VAT is added on top of the net base. On a €100 net item at 20% VAT, the gross price is €120. Removing 20% VAT means dividing €120 by 1.20 to get back to €100 (€20 VAT), whereas 120 × 0.80 would wrongly give €96."
    },
    {
      "q": "When does EU B2B reverse charge (0% VAT) apply?",
      "a": "Cross-border B2B sales between VAT-registered businesses in two different EU member states typically use the reverse charge mechanism where the invoice carries 0% VAT and the buyer accounts for VAT locally."
    }
